1
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:07,250
♪By red walls and a dry well,
my crown gathers dust and frost♪

2
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:11,860
♪With a hoe and a patch of wasteland,
I sow the moonlight♪

3
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:16,120
♪Who says the Cold Palace
holds nothing but tears?♪

4
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:20,330
♪I choose to fill it with fragrant wine♪

5
00:00:20,670 --> 00:00:22,200
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

6
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:24,730
♪Growing life's simple joys♪

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,880
♪Bins full of grain, jars full of wine♪

8
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:28,760
♪Better than dancing in silks♪

9
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:30,650
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

10
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:33,320
♪My heart longs for the world beyond♪

11
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:35,800
♪Tending a courtyard full of life♪

12
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:40,560
♪Come, share a cup with me♪

13
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:42,540
(Welcome to Cold Palace Refreshments)

14
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:47,040
=Farm Busily in the Cold Palace=

15
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,620
(Based on Hongshu.com's novel
I'm Busy Farming in the Cold Palace)

16
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:49,650
=Episode 21=

17
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:53,719
Your Majesty is so blessed,

18
00:00:53,719 --> 00:00:56,520
even the underworld must yield to you.

19
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:58,880
How is Shangyuan now?

20
00:00:59,399 --> 00:01:00,759
Your Majesty,

21
00:01:00,799 --> 00:01:02,399
nine in ten homes stand empty.

22
00:01:02,399 --> 00:01:03,000
The city...

23
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:07,280
has been sealed for ten days.

24
00:01:08,239 --> 00:01:11,120
Sire, the Emperor Star has shifted.

25
00:01:11,439 --> 00:01:13,480
The Phoenix Star shines in the heavens.

26
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,680
This is a sign from Heaven.

27
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:18,920
I've divined our nation's fate.

28
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:20,719
The epidemic in Shangyuan

29
00:01:20,719 --> 00:01:25,239
only the Empress's presence can quell
Heaven's wrath.

30
00:01:26,799 --> 00:01:29,120
How does he know she can cure it?

31
00:01:29,519 --> 00:01:31,040
Did he really divine it?

32
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:31,879
Absurd!

33
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:34,640
Even all the imperial physicians are
helpless!

34
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:37,120
You dare put the Empress in danger?

35
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:38,959
The trigrams are clear.

36
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:42,120
The Empress herself must go.

37
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,959
It is Heaven's will.

38
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,599
What utter rubbish!

39
00:01:45,599 --> 00:01:47,920
During the drought, you made His Majesty
kneel at the altar!

40
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,760
Now you want to send the Empress to her
death in an epidemic!

41
00:01:51,359 --> 00:01:54,400
Why does the Imperial Observatory always
target the royal family?

42
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:57,760
Your Majesty.

43
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:00,519
He visited Ningxin Palace yesterday.

44
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,280
(Heaven's will?)

45
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:05,239
(More like the Empress Dowager's.)

46
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,560
(Yunluo intends to go anyway.)

47
00:02:07,879 --> 00:02:09,319
(I may as well play along.)

48
00:02:09,319 --> 00:02:10,560
Heaven's will, indeed.

49
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,080
Then ask Heaven this for me.

50
00:02:14,199 --> 00:02:17,240
If the Empress ends this epidemic,

51
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,560
what honor should she receive?

52
00:02:18,719 --> 00:02:20,120
(The Empress Dowager only said)

53
00:02:20,159 --> 00:02:22,000
(that witch was certain to die.)

54
00:02:24,479 --> 00:02:26,240
Such a feat deserves a living shrine

55
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:29,120
and a place in the Ancestral Temple,

56
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:31,080
with offerings for all eternity.

57
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:32,719
Very well.

58
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:36,719
The Empress shall go in Heaven's name

59
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,599
on my behalf.

60
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,159
Your Majesty is wise.

61
00:02:41,759 --> 00:02:44,120
Since you can discern Heaven's will,

62
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:48,039
who better to read the stars

63
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,719
and foretell what awaits her?

64
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:51,120
By my command,

65
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:54,120
the Director of the Imperial Observatory
shall accompany her.

66
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,039
Your...

67
00:02:55,039 --> 00:02:55,719
Your Majesty!

68
00:02:55,719 --> 00:02:57,759
I know nothing of medicine.

69
00:02:57,759 --> 00:02:59,520
I'd only be a burden!

70
00:03:00,159 --> 00:03:00,960
Oh?

71
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:05,840
Yet you know the Empress can heal?

72
00:03:06,919 --> 00:03:08,840
It's Heaven's will.

73
00:03:08,879 --> 00:03:10,879
Then let Heaven protect you.

74
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,159
Your Majesty!

75
00:03:12,159 --> 00:03:14,680
My legs are frail.

76
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:16,840
I'd delay the journey!

77
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:17,680
Your Majesty.

78
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:20,879
I request more Blacksteel Guard troops
to escort the Empress.

79
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:23,879
Ha.

80
00:03:23,879 --> 00:03:25,280
Frail legs?

81
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:26,759
They'll carry you.

82
00:03:26,759 --> 00:03:27,039
You!

83
00:03:27,039 --> 00:03:27,719
Granted.

84
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:30,680
Set out in three days.

85
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:34,120
Open Zhuque Gate. All officials shall
kneel to see her off.

86
00:03:35,199 --> 00:03:38,719
A wise emperor and a virtuous empress!

87
00:03:38,719 --> 00:03:42,159
May Heaven bless Donglan and its people!

88
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:45,879
Long live Your Majesty!

89
00:03:47,439 --> 00:03:48,800
(The people's hearts)

90
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:51,199
(are where true hope lies.)

91
00:03:52,879 --> 00:03:55,199
(10,000 taels)
Have Matron get banknotes for it.

92
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:57,000
Pack a couple of changes of clothes.

93
00:03:57,879 --> 00:03:59,400
We'll travel light.

94
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,599
Your Highness.

95
00:04:04,319 --> 00:04:06,520
Hundreds die in Shangyuan every day.

96
00:04:06,919 --> 00:04:07,599
You...

97
00:04:07,599 --> 00:04:10,199
You're walking into death's jaws!

98
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:12,319
If anything happens to you...

99
00:04:12,719 --> 00:04:13,599
When His Majesty fell ill,

100
00:04:13,599 --> 00:04:15,280
wasn't nursing him day and night enough?

101
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,720
Someone is trying to kill you!

102
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,920
I'll see His Majesty at once.

103
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:18,800
Wait.

104
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:21,800
I've found a way to prevent smallpox.

105
00:04:22,959 --> 00:04:23,759
Here.

106
00:04:25,079 --> 00:04:26,439
(Cowpox: Collection)
Here's the method.

107
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,439
(Prepare; Inoculate)
The Medical Office will adopt it soon.

108
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:29,360
Really?

109
00:04:29,639 --> 00:04:30,879
Have I ever lied to you?

110
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:32,720
You're truly remarkable, sister.

111
00:04:33,079 --> 00:04:34,720
If you hadn't married His Majesty,

112
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,120
I'd take you to Liu to marry my brother.

113
00:04:37,519 --> 00:04:38,600
That's no obstacle.

114
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:39,360
Is he handsome?

115
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,879
He's among the five nations'

116
00:04:41,879 --> 00:04:43,279
ten most handsome men.

117
00:04:43,279 --> 00:04:44,000
Ooh!

118
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,120
Then save him for me!

119
00:04:45,319 --> 00:04:46,319
We've got plenty of time.

120
00:04:54,439 --> 00:04:56,720
Sister, you're already here,

121
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,839
and you brought all this too?

122
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:04,240
I hear you're leaving for Shangyuan.

123
00:05:04,439 --> 00:05:06,000
The epidemic is raging there.

124
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:08,759
Do take care.

125
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:12,120
What are you up to now?

126
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:15,040
Well, since you're leaving,

127
00:05:15,319 --> 00:05:17,399
and anything could happen,

128
00:05:17,399 --> 00:05:19,279
you might never return.

129
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:21,240
Why don't I move in?

130
00:05:21,519 --> 00:05:24,000
I can take over your Cold Palace shops

131
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,079
and look after your wheat.

132
00:05:26,959 --> 00:05:29,600
You're hoping I'll die out there?

133
00:05:29,639 --> 00:05:31,399
How could you say that?

134
00:05:31,399 --> 00:05:34,920
The Cold Palace has always terrified
imperial consorts.

135
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,480
You're the first

136
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,120
who's been so eager to move in.

137
00:05:39,519 --> 00:05:40,600
With all that luggage,

138
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:43,040
people might think you packed a coffin.

139
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,040
You!

140
00:05:47,839 --> 00:05:50,120
Your Highness, it's time to leave.

141
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:53,600
Stay here if you want.

142
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:56,160
But that wheat is vital to our nation.

143
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,439
(Farming Manual)
I wrote this.

144
00:05:58,639 --> 00:06:00,319
It must go to the Director of the
Agriculture Office.

145
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:02,759
Record the wheat's growth every day.

146
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:04,560
Pest control is on page seventeen.

147
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:05,720
Wheat likes dry soil.

148
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,279
Don't overwater it.

149
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,279
Don't worry.

150
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:11,160
I'll take good care of it.

151
00:06:14,199 --> 00:06:15,319
(I've lived here so long.)

152
00:06:15,759 --> 00:06:17,560
(I put everything here myself.)

153
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,199
(It's hard to leave.)

154
00:06:22,639 --> 00:06:23,680
Your Highness,

155
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,000
the auspicious hour has arrived.

156
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:26,600
All right.

157
00:06:44,439 --> 00:06:46,720
What a pleasant little courtyard.

158
00:06:47,399 --> 00:06:48,680
From now on,

159
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,560
it's all mine.

160
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,439
Your Highness, what about this manual?

161
00:06:53,439 --> 00:06:54,319
Burn it.

162
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,279
Use it to boil water

163
00:06:56,279 --> 00:06:58,560
for a fresh pot of tea.

164
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,040
Yes, Your Highness.

165
00:07:08,959 --> 00:07:09,800
Ah.

166
00:07:10,839 --> 00:07:12,600
If you'll miss her so much,

167
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:15,000
why not see her off yourself?

168
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:16,959
I'm afraid

169
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:20,920
I'm afraid I'll regret it,

170
00:07:22,519 --> 00:07:23,800
and won't be able to let her go.

171
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,600
You mean...

172
00:07:28,199 --> 00:07:29,319
I promised her,

173
00:07:30,399 --> 00:07:32,519
once the epidemic in Shangyuan ends,

174
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:34,639
she'll have her freedom.

175
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,399
She won't be coming back.

176
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,160
Alas.

177
00:07:41,959 --> 00:07:44,079
Why put yourself through this?

178
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:51,000
She's done more than enough.

179
00:07:52,279 --> 00:07:58,079
Fish leap in open seas; birds soar in
boundless skies.

180
00:08:06,199 --> 00:08:08,000
One of us trapped here

181
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,519
is enough.

182
00:08:11,839 --> 00:08:12,639
Alas.

183
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:22,480
- Reporting back, Your Majesty.
- Reporting back, Your Majesty.

184
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,439
The Empress has left.

185
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:28,560
Return to your former posts.

186
00:08:29,199 --> 00:08:30,199
Your Majesty,

187
00:08:30,199 --> 00:08:31,279
we both

188
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:32,919
have a favor to ask.

189
00:08:37,279 --> 00:08:38,679
We wish to stay with her

190
00:08:38,679 --> 00:08:39,799
and go to Shangyuan.

191
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,200
Who was it

192
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,279
said it was beneath them

193
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:52,600
and grudgingly took the job of guarding
the Cold Palace?

194
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:57,919
Go.

195
00:08:59,639 --> 00:09:00,440
For me,

196
00:09:01,799 --> 00:09:02,759
keep her safe.

197
00:09:03,919 --> 00:09:04,759
- Thank you, Your Majesty!
- Thank you, Your Majesty!

198
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:23,919
My lady,

199
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:26,639
Matron Zhou found us a house and a shop.

200
00:09:27,159 --> 00:09:29,039
Once we arrive, we can...

201
00:09:29,039 --> 00:09:29,639
Ahem.

202
00:09:31,559 --> 00:09:32,679
Your backside still sore?

203
00:09:32,679 --> 00:09:33,759
I'm fine!

204
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:35,519
The saddle just chafed my legs.

205
00:09:35,759 --> 00:09:36,919
The physician treated them.

206
00:09:38,559 --> 00:09:39,360
Ah!

207
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:45,960
Ow!

208
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:49,799
My leg is cramping again!

209
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:52,679
Sleeping rough all this way,

210
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:56,360
I've nearly fallen off my horse several
times!

211
00:09:56,799 --> 00:09:59,159
Could you make an exception

212
00:09:59,440 --> 00:10:01,799
and find me a sedan too?

213
00:10:04,399 --> 00:10:06,039
Aren't you good at divination?

214
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,200
Fly there on your sword!

215
00:10:08,159 --> 00:10:09,360
Your... Your Highness!

216
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,039
My compass is cracked!

217
00:10:14,279 --> 00:10:15,840
It's a seven-day journey,

218
00:10:16,039 --> 00:10:17,879
that old fool took 10 days, and we're
not there!

219
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,120
You look so delicate,

220
00:10:20,159 --> 00:10:22,159
but you've really opened my ears.

221
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:23,840
Eyes.

222
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,399
You've really eared my eyes.

223
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:26,919
Opened my eyes.

224
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:27,759
Forget it.

225
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,480
Let's move on.

226
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,600
Something serious now.

227
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,559
Shangyuan is your fief, right?

228
00:10:33,639 --> 00:10:34,799
We enter the city tomorrow.

229
00:10:35,519 --> 00:10:36,799
Tell me about it.

230
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:40,600
The outbreak is in Tailing County,
Shangyuan.

231
00:10:40,879 --> 00:10:42,200
It was first detected over 20 days ago.

232
00:10:42,559 --> 00:10:45,720
The court has received reports of over
10,000 deaths.

233
00:10:47,919 --> 00:10:50,039
They couldn't all have died so suddenly.

234
00:10:51,919 --> 00:10:53,360
This disease may be deadly,

235
00:10:53,559 --> 00:10:55,120
but it still takes time to spread.

236
00:10:55,679 --> 00:10:56,639
My lady,

237
00:10:56,639 --> 00:10:59,080
you think someone hid the outbreak,

238
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,000
until they couldn't cover it up?

239
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,559
Who's Tailing County's magistrate?

240
00:11:03,639 --> 00:11:05,360
The magistrate?

241
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:07,000
Cao something.

242
00:11:07,399 --> 00:11:07,759
Oh.

243
00:11:07,759 --> 00:11:09,080
I can't remember.

244
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:12,200
Luckily, my uncle is in Tailing County.

245
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:13,240
Prince Chen?

246
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:13,720
Yes.

247
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:15,919
On his second day in Tailing County,

248
00:11:15,919 --> 00:11:17,159
he ordered the city sealed.

249
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:18,879
He's an excellent physician,

250
00:11:18,879 --> 00:11:21,279
and faced the epidemic ten years ago.

251
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:23,600
He tested medicine on himself for them.

252
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:25,039
The people respect him deeply.

253
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:27,360
So

254
00:11:27,799 --> 00:11:31,320
his illness dates back to that epidemic.

255
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:57,670
♪By red walls and a dry well,
my crown gathers dust and frost♪

256
00:11:58,060 --> 00:12:02,280
♪With a hoe and a patch of wasteland,
I sow the moonlight♪

257
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:06,500
♪Who says the Cold Palace
holds nothing but tears?♪

258
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:10,750
♪I choose to fill it with fragrant wine♪

259
00:12:11,090 --> 00:12:15,150
♪Cool dew, starry nights,
wheat sprouts in my hands♪

260
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:19,400
♪I shape fields, not painted brows,
and fill them with hope♪

261
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:23,210
♪Gold and silver bloom from the soil♪

262
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:28,360
♪I smile as the world storms on♪

263
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:32,170
♪No finery to rival spring♪

264
00:12:32,350 --> 00:12:36,650
♪All I wish for are waves of green♪

265
00:12:39,060 --> 00:12:40,810
♪Where is beauty found?♪

266
00:12:40,990 --> 00:12:45,420
♪Just lift your eyes and see♪

267
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:47,550
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

268
00:12:47,570 --> 00:12:50,040
♪Growing life's simple joys♪

269
00:12:50,110 --> 00:12:52,190
♪Bins full of grain, jars full of wine♪

270
00:12:52,350 --> 00:12:54,120
♪Better than dancing in silks♪

271
00:12:54,730 --> 00:12:56,000
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

272
00:12:56,230 --> 00:12:58,630
♪My heart longs for the world beyond♪

273
00:12:58,870 --> 00:13:01,170
♪Tending a courtyard full of life♪

274
00:13:01,450 --> 00:13:05,770
♪Come, share a cup with me♪
